/F2 20 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 720 Tm (The Lighthouse at Marrow Point) Tj
/F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 678 Tm (Every evening, just before the sky turned the colour of cold tea,) Tj
/F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 661 Tm (Ada climbed the one hundred and twelve steps of the lighthouse at) Tj
/F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 644 Tm (Marrow Point. She counted them out of habit, not need. The steps had) Tj
/F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 627 Tm (not changed in forty years, and neither, she suspected, had she.) Tj
/F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 604 Tm (The lamp was older than the town. It had been shipped over in) Tj
/F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 587 Tm (pieces, bolted together by men whose names were now only scratches) Tj
/F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 570 Tm (on the brass. Ada polished the lens each morning with a cloth her) Tj
/F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 553 Tm (mother had used, and each morning the glass gave back her face,) Tj
/F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 536 Tm (stretched and curious.) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 60 Tm (Page 1 of 4) Tj
