/F2 20 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 720 Tm (Chapter Two) Tj
/F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 678 Tm (The first boat that did not come was the Kestrel. Ada watched for) Tj
/F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 661 Tm (its green lantern until the tide turned and the wind carried the) Tj
/F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 644 Tm (smell of rain up from the rocks. She logged the hour, the weather,) Tj
/F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 627 Tm (and the absence, because absence was still something that could be) Tj
/F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 610 Tm (written down.) Tj
/F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 587 Tm (In the morning the harbour master rowed out with news. The Kestrel) Tj
/F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 570 Tm (had put in at Salt Haven instead, its captain spooked by a fog that) Tj
/F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 553 Tm (Ada had not seen from the tower. She wrote that down as well. It was) Tj
/F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 536 Tm (the first time the sea had kept a secret from her.) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 60 Tm (Page 2 of 4) Tj
