/F2 20 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 720 Tm (Chapter Three) Tj
/F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 678 Tm (Winter arrived with the patience of something that knows it will be) Tj
/F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 661 Tm (staying. Ada wrapped the pipes, stacked the coal, and taught herself) Tj
/F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 644 Tm (to read the weather from the way gulls sat on the railings. When) Tj
/F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 627 Tm (they faced the land, she lit the lamp early.) Tj
/F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 604 Tm (On the longest night she found a boy on the steps, soaked and) Tj
/F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 587 Tm (shivering, who said he had followed the light. She did not ask from) Tj
/F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 570 Tm (where. She gave him soup, a blanket, and the job of counting the) Tj
/F1 12 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 553 Tm (steps, which he got wrong three times before breakfast.) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 1 0 0 1 72 60 Tm (Page 3 of 4) Tj
